  "question": {
    "text": "Let $\\mathrm{I}=\\int_{\\pi / 4}^{\\pi / 3} \\frac{\\sin \\mathrm{x}}{\\mathrm{x}} \\mathrm{dx}$. Then"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{8} \\leq \\mathrm{I} \\leq \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{6}$",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2 \\pi} \\leq \\mathrm{I} \\leq \\frac{2 \\sqrt{3}}{\\pi}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{9} \\leq \\mathrm{I} \\leq \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{16}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\pi \\leq \\mathrm{I} \\leq \\frac{4 \\pi}{3}$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$f(x)=\\frac{\\sin x}{x}$ (decreasing function)\r\n$\\Rightarrow f\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{3}\\right)     < f(x) < f\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)$\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\times \\frac{3}{\\pi} \\int_{\\pi / 4}^{\\pi / 3} d x < I < \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\times \\frac{4}{\\pi} \\times \\int_{\\pi / 4}^{\\pi / 3} d x$\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{8} < I < \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{6}$"
  }
}